 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? That's a wonderful way to explore the city without having to own a bike. Which city is it? You pay for time you spend on the bike, usually an hour or half hour, and lock it to a post. No, for shared dock systems they expect you to log bike in before you leave. There' often a little screen on each dock for this. Back, and the system tells you when you've logged the bike in. Best tip is to log it in right before you lock it. The system doesn't care, and it helps with capacity planning. Lots of people do, five or ten rides a week. Shopping, seeing friends, getting exercise.",
